-- title:
--   The annealing schedule factor is nonnegative on every ground size
-- statement:
--   Let $n\in\mathbb N$ and let $p=(\varepsilon,\delta)\in\mathbb Q^2$ satisfy $0<\varepsilon,\delta<1$. The computed schedule has rational factor
--   $$\rho=1-\frac1{2n},$$
--   using total rational division, so $1/0=0$. Then
--   $$\rho\ge0.$$
--   In particular the conclusion includes $n=0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ScheduleResourceEnvelope.lean#L13-L30

